const LEASE_TPL = {"NJ": "RESIDENTIAL LEASE AGREEMENT (New Jersey)\n\nREVIEW WITH YOUR ATTORNEY BEFORE USE. This template is a starting point, not legal advice.\n\n1. PARTIES. This Lease is between {{landlord}} (\"Landlord\") and {{tenant_names}} (\"Tenant\").\n\n2. PREMISES. Landlord rents to Tenant the residence at {{property_address}}{{unit_text}}, {{city_state}} (the \"Premises\").\n\n3. TERM. The Lease begins on {{start}} and ends on {{end}}. If Tenant stays after the end date with Landlord's consent and no new lease is signed, the tenancy continues month to month on the same terms.\n\n4. RENT. Monthly rent is {{rent}}, due on the {{due_day}} day of each month, without demand. Rent can be paid by {{pay_methods}}. {{other_charges}}\n\n5. LATE CHARGE. If rent is not received by the end of the grace period ({{grace_days}} days after the due date), Tenant will pay a late charge of {{late_fee_text}}. If Tenant is a senior citizen receiving Social Security, SSI, or another pension or benefit described in N.J.S.A. 2A:42-6.1, the grace period is five business days.\n\n6. SECURITY DEPOSIT. Tenant pays a security deposit of {{deposit}}, which may not exceed one and one-half months' rent (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2). Landlord will hold the deposit as required by the Rent Security Deposit Act and tell Tenant in writing where it is held and how much interest it earns. Within 30 days after the Lease ends, Landlord will return the deposit plus interest, minus any lawful deductions, with an itemized list (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).\n\n7. UTILITIES. Tenant pays for: {{utilities_tenant}}. Landlord pays for all other utilities serving the Premises.\n\n8. USE AND OCCUPANCY. The Premises may be used only as a private residence by Tenant and these occupants: {{occupants}}. No assignment or sublet without Landlord's written consent.\n\n9. CARE OF THE PREMISES. Tenant will keep the Premises clean and safe, will not damage them, and will promptly report needed repairs (the tenant repair link or portal may be used). Tenant pays to repair damage caused by Tenant, household members or guests, beyond normal wear and tear.\n\n10. REPAIRS AND ACCESS. Landlord will keep the Premises fit to live in and make needed repairs within a reasonable time. Landlord may enter at reasonable times with reasonable advance notice to inspect, repair or show the Premises, and at any time in an emergency.\n\n11. PETS. {{pets}}\n\n12. SMOKE AND CARBON MONOXIDE ALARMS. Landlord has installed working smoke and carbon monoxide alarms where required. Tenant will test them, replace batteries as needed, and not disable them.\n\n13. RULES AND LAWS. Tenant will obey all laws and reasonable building rules and will not disturb neighbors.\n\n14. LEAD-BASED PAINT. If the building was built before 1978, Tenant acknowledges receiving the federal lead-based paint disclosure and the EPA pamphlet \"Protect Your Family From Lead in Your Home.\"\n\n15. FLOOD RISK. Landlord has given Tenant the flood-risk disclosure required by N.J.S.A. 46:8-50, stating whether the Premises are in a FEMA flood zone and any known flood damage.\n\n16. TRUTH IN RENTING. Tenant acknowledges receiving the New Jersey \"Truth in Renting\" guide where required (N.J.S.A. 46:8-45 et seq.).\n\n17. ENDING THE LEASE AND EVICTION. Landlord may only evict Tenant for a cause allowed by the New Jersey Anti-Eviction Act (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1) and only through the court.\n\n18. NOTICES. Notices to Landlord go to {{landlord}}{{office_contact}}. Notices to Tenant go to the Premises.\n\n19. ENTIRE AGREEMENT. This Lease is the entire agreement. Changes must be in writing and signed by both parties. If any part is invalid, the rest stays in effect.\n\n20. ELECTRONIC SIGNATURES. The parties agree to sign this Lease electronically. Electronic signatures have the same effect as handwritten signatures.\n", "OH": "RESIDENTIAL LEASE AGREEMENT (Ohio)\n\nREVIEW WITH YOUR ATTORNEY BEFORE USE. This template is a starting point, not legal advice.\n\n1. PARTIES. This Lease is between {{landlord}} (\"Landlord\") and {{tenant_names}} (\"Tenant\").\n\n2. PREMISES. Landlord rents to Tenant the residence at {{property_address}}{{unit_text}}, {{city_state}} (the \"Premises\").\n\n3. TERM. The Lease begins on {{start}} and ends on {{end}}. If Tenant stays after the end date with Landlord's consent and no new lease is signed, the tenancy continues month to month on the same terms.\n\n4. RENT. Monthly rent is {{rent}}, due on the {{due_day}} day of each month, without demand. Rent can be paid by {{pay_methods}}. {{other_charges}}\n\n5. LATE CHARGE. If rent is not received by the end of the grace period ({{grace_days}} days after the due date), Tenant will pay a late charge of {{late_fee_text}}.\n\n6. SECURITY DEPOSIT. Tenant pays a security deposit of {{deposit}}. Within 30 days after Tenant moves out and returns possession, Landlord will return the deposit, minus lawful deductions, with an itemized written list of any deductions, mailed to the forwarding address Tenant gives in writing (Ohio Revised Code 5321.16). If required by that section, Landlord will pay interest on the deposit.\n\n7. UTILITIES. Tenant pays for: {{utilities_tenant}}. Landlord pays for all other utilities serving the Premises.\n\n8. USE AND OCCUPANCY. The Premises may be used only as a private residence by Tenant and these occupants: {{occupants}}. No assignment or sublet without Landlord's written consent.\n\n9. TENANT DUTIES. Tenant will keep the Premises safe and sanitary, dispose of garbage properly, keep plumbing fixtures clean, use appliances and systems properly, not damage the Premises, and comply with applicable housing codes (O.R.C. 5321.05). Tenant will promptly report needed repairs (the tenant repair link or portal may be used).\n\n10. LANDLORD DUTIES AND ACCESS. Landlord will comply with O.R.C. 5321.04, keep the Premises fit and habitable, and make repairs. Except in an emergency, Landlord will give at least 24 hours' notice before entering, and will enter at reasonable times.\n\n11. PETS. {{pets}}\n\n12. SMOKE AND CARBON MONOXIDE ALARMS. Landlord has installed working smoke alarms (and carbon monoxide alarms where required). Tenant will test them, replace batteries as needed, and not disable them.\n\n13. RULES AND LAWS. Tenant will obey all laws and reasonable rules and will not disturb neighbors.\n\n14. LEAD-BASED PAINT. If the building was built before 1978, Tenant acknowledges receiving the federal lead-based paint disclosure and the EPA pamphlet \"Protect Your Family From Lead in Your Home.\"\n\n15. ENDING THE LEASE. Either party may end a month-to-month tenancy with at least 30 days' written notice before the end of a rental period. Eviction may only happen through the court.\n\n16. NOTICES. Notices to Landlord go to {{landlord}}{{office_contact}}. Notices to Tenant go to the Premises.\n\n17. ENTIRE AGREEMENT. This Lease is the entire agreement. Changes must be in writing and signed by both parties. If any part is invalid, the rest stays in effect.\n\n18. ELECTRONIC SIGNATURES. The parties agree to sign this Lease electronically. Electronic signatures have the same effect as handwritten signatures.\n"};
